{
  "format": "sfxgen/1",
  "name": "Warp jump",
  "description": "A starship jumps to light speed, heard from just behind it. First space is pulled in: the ring of a huge struck hull plate played backwards in a cathedral-sized reverb, swelling out of nothing, while the drive's chord is stretched upward through a jet-like flanger. Then the jump, the loudest thing in the sound: a slammed low boom with a cracking front edge and a roar of torn air that falls quickly from bright to dark. After it the ship is already gone: its wake tears away past you (noise with real Doppler) and the boom rolls off into empty space.",
  "tags": ["scifi", "warp", "hyperspace", "jump", "spaceship", "ftl", "whoosh", "boom", "riser"],
  "duration": "auto",
  "seed": 21,
  "output": {
    "channels": 2
  },
  "tracks": [
    {
      "id": "inhale",
      "note": "The suck-in: a metal plate hit, drowned in reverb, faded to nothing right at the jump and then reversed, so it swells from silence over the whole build and stops dead at the jump.",
